WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:03.378 align:start position:0% line:0%
So there are seven main
petals that form the core of

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:04.879 line:0%
The Living Building Challenge.

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:08.800
The first has to do with place,
understanding the climate

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.594
and impacts that a building
may have on its site.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.723
The second has to do
with the responsible use

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.600
of energy on site
as well as water.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:20.019
Then there's
the use of materials.

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:20.687
And here

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:24.441
the focus is to eliminate all of
these chemicals and materials

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.483
that are known

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.695
to be destructive,
either in terms of toxicity,

00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:32.574
energy, or depletion
of resources around the world.

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:33.783
And lastly,

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.618
there's a whole slew
of really interesting

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:39.706
criteria, including happiness
and well-being, equity,

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.792
and this wonderful category
called biophilic design.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.920
And that really opens up
an aspirational aspect

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.839
of The Living Building
Challenge,

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:51.009
which is to connect humans
with their broader ecology.

